{"Docs":[{"DocType":1,"IsAmended":false,"IsUpdated":false,"CompareStatus":4,"DocOrderId":62,"AmendedBy":[],"Notes":[],"Drafts":[],"ChunkGroupStartingNodeId":"PTIISTPECO_CH1GEPR","NodeDepth":2,"TitleHtml":"<div class=\"chunk-title\">Sec. 1-2. - Definitions and rules of construction.</div>","ShouldShowMiniToc":false,"Id":"PTIISTPECO_CH1GEPR_S1-2DERUCO","Title":"Sec. 1-2. - Definitions and rules of construction.","Content":"<div class=\"chunk-content\">\n            <p class=\"incr0\">\n               (a)\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"content1\">\n               In the construction of this Code the following definitions and rules apply unless\n               inconsistent with the manifest intent of the City Council:\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Agencies, officers.</span> Any reference to any local, State or federal agency or officer includes any successor\n               agency or officer.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Charter.</span> The term \"Charter\" means the Charter of the City of St. Petersburg, Florida, and\n               any amendments thereto, a copy of which is printed in part I of this volume.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">City.</span> The term \"City\" means the City of St. Petersburg, Florida.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">City Council.</span> The term \"City Council\" means the City Council of the City of St. Petersburg.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Code.</span> The term \"Code\" means the St. Petersburg City Code.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Computation of time.</span> In computing any period of time prescribed or allowed by ordinance or Code, the day\n               of the act, event or default from which the designated period of time begins to run\n               is not included. The last day of the period so computed is included unless it is a\n               Saturday, Sunday or a day when the City Clerk's office is closed in which event the\n               period runs until the end of the next day which is neither a Saturday, Sunday or a\n               day when the City Clerk's office is closed. When the period of time prescribed or\n               allowed is less than seven days, intermediate Saturdays, Sundays and a day when the\n               City Clerk's office is closed are excluded from the computation.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">County.</span> The term \"county\" means Pinellas County, Florida.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Delegation of authority.</span> Whenever a provision of this Code requires or authorizes a City officer or a City\n               employee to do some act or perform some duty, it shall be construed to authorize the\n               officer or employee to designate, delegate and authorize another employee to perform\n               the act or duty or to contract with another to perform the act or duty.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">F.A.C.</span> The term \"F.A.C.\" refers to the Florida Administrative Code, as may be amended or\n               revised from time to time.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Filing, filed</span> and <span class=\"ital\">file.</span> The terms \"filing,\" \"filed\" and \"file,\" when used to indicate the filing of some\n               item with the City, mean the actual receipt of the item to be filed which item has\n               been delivered by hand-delivery, confirmed facsimile delivery or U.S. mail or courier\n               service. For the filing to be effective, delivery shall be to the official or place\n               designated in the ordinance or Code or if no official or place is so designated, delivery\n               shall be to the City Clerk. Delivery by email or other electronic means except confirmed\n               facsimile shall not be deemed effective.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">F.S.</span> The term \"F.S.\" or \"Florida Statutes\" refers to the latest edition of the Florida\n               Statutes adopted by law, as the same may be amended from time to time. A reference\n               to a section or chapter of the Florida Statutes which is later renumbered, or transferred\n               to another section or chapter of the Florida Statutes and renumbered, means and includes\n               the section or chapter after such change.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Gender.</span> Words used in one gender apply also to the other genders.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Health department.</span> The term \"health department\" means the county health department.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Health officer.</span> The term \"health officer\" means the county health officer or designee.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Interpretation.</span> In the interpretation and application of any provision, it shall be held to be the\n               minimum requirements adopted for the promotion of the public health, safety, comfort,\n               convenience and general welfare. Where any provision imposes greater restrictions\n               upon the subject matter than the general provisions imposed by the Code, the provision\n               imposing the greater restriction or regulation shall be controlling.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Keeper</span> or<span class=\"ital\">proprietor.</span> The term \"keeper\" or \"proprietor\" includes a person acting alone or through a servant,\n               agent or employee.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">May.</span> The term \"may\" is to be construed as being permissive.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Month.</span> The term \"month\" means a calendar month.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Municipal pier </span>means the overwater structure defined in City Charter subsection <a href=\"\" data-chunk-id=\"PTICH_ARTIPO_S1.02PAWAPRUSDI\" class=\"section-link\" data-product-id=\"14674\">1.02</a>(c)(4)(B).\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Municipal pier approach </span>means the municipal pier uplands east of the seawall abutting Bayshore Drive, including\n               the following parcels on City Park and Waterfront Map: the Pier Parking Area (G),\n               the Historic Museum Area (C), and Spa Beach (30).\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Municipal pier district </span>means, collectively, (i) the municipal pier; (ii) the municipal pier approach; and\n               (iii) the municipal pier gateway.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Municipal pier gateway</span> means the entry plaza to the municipal pier district located along 2nd Avenue Northeast,\n               between the eastern right-of-way line of Beach Drive and the western boundary of the\n               municipal pier approach.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Must.</span> The term \"must\" is to be construed as being mandatory.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Newspaper of general circulation in the City.</span> The term \"newspaper of general circulation in the City\" means, for the limited purpose\n               of determining whether a periodical may be used to publish a notice to the public,\n               any newspaper having circulation within the City which meets the applicable criteria\n               set forth in F.S. ch. 50 or 163, or in any other provision of law defining the term\n               for that purpose. For any other purpose, the term \"newspaper\" shall have its ordinary\n               and commonly understood meaning which may include but is not limited to any handbill\n               or other publication whether or not the publication qualifies for the publication\n               of notices to the public.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Nontechnical and technical words.</span> Words and phrases shall be construed according to the common and approved usage of\n               the language, but technical words and phrases and such others as may have acquired\n               a peculiar and appropriate meaning in law shall be construed and understood according\n               to such meaning.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Number.</span> Words used in the singular number include the plural and the plural includes the\n               singular.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Oath.</span> The term \"oath\" includes an affirmation in all cases in which, by law, an affirmation\n               may be substituted for an oath, and in such cases the terms \"swear\" and \"sworn\" are\n               equivalent to the terms \"affirm\" and \"affirmed.\"\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Officers, Officials, etc.</span> Whenever reference is made to Officials, Boards, Commissions, etc., by title only,\n               i.e., \"City Administration\" or \"City Clerk\" it shall be deemed to refer to Officials,\n               Boards, Commissions, etc., of the City.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Or, and.</span> The term \"or\" may be read \"and\" if the sense requires it. The term \"and\" may be read\n               \"or\" if the sense requires it.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Owner.</span> The term \"owner,\" as applied to the whole or part of a building or land, includes\n               any part owner, joint owner, tenant in common, tenant in partnership, joint tenant\n               or tenant by the entirety.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Person.</span> The term \"person\" includes individuals, children, firms, associations, joint ventures,\n               partnerships, estates, trusts, business trusts, syndicates, fiduciaries, corporations\n               and all other entities, groups or combinations.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Personal property.</span> The term \"personal property\" includes every species of property except real property.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">POD.</span> The term \"POD\" means the person officially designated by the Mayor to perform the\n               duties described in that portion of the Code.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Property.</span> The term \"property\" includes real and personal property.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Real property.</span> The term \"real property\" includes lands, tenements and hereditaments.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Shall.</span> The term \"shall\" is to be construed as being mandatory.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">State.</span> The term \"State\" means the State of Florida.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Street.</span> The term \"street\" means any street, avenue, boulevard, road, alley, lane, viaduct\n               or other public highway in the City.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Tenant</span> or <span class=\"ital\">occupant.</span> The term \"tenant\" or \"occupant,\" as applied to a building or land, includes any person\n               holding a written or oral lease of or who occupies the whole or a part of such building\n               or land, either alone or with others.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Tense.</span> Words used in the past or present tense include the future tense.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Written, in writing.</span> The term \"written\" or \"in writing\" includes typewriting, printing on paper and any\n               other mode of representing words and letters.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Year.</span> The term \"year\" means a calendar year.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               Any reference to a specific code, section, subsection, article, chapter, etc. of the\n               City, County, State, United States, or any other governmental entity, or to an official\n               publication which establishes standards to be followed or best practices, shall mean\n               and include, \"as amended.\"\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"incr0\">\n               (b)\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"content1\">\n               Whenever any portion of the Code specifies the need for an approval, a determination,\n               the issuance of permits, or the review or promulgation of standards or criteria, said\n               approval, determination, review, permitting, or promulgation shall be the duty and\n               responsibility of the POD unless otherwise specifically provided. Such approvals,\n               determinations, reviews, decisions to permit and promulgations of standards and criteria\n               shall be based upon the requirements of the Code and generally accepted scientific\n               concepts and professional standards, and any applicable federal, State and other City\n               regulations.\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"historynote0\">\n               (Code 1973, § 1-2; Code 1992, § 1-2; Ord. No. 2027-F, § 1, 1-3-1991; Ord. No. 130-G,\n               § 1, 4-7-1994; Ord. No. 548-G, § 1, 9-5-2002; Ord. No. 141-H, § 5, 11-24-2014; Ord.\n               No. 357-H, § 2(a), 1-3-2019; Ord. No. 407-H, § 3, 12-5-2019)\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"refstatelaw0\" block_type=\"hang\"><b>State Law reference— </b>\n               Construction of statutes, F.S. § 1.01 et seq.\n               </p></div>","SortDate":null,"Footnotes":null}],"NewOrds":[],"PdfUrl":null,"LastOrd":null,"PrevNode":{"Id":"PTIISTPECO_CH1GEPR_S1-1HOCODECI","Heading":"Sec. 1-1. - How Code designated and cited.","NodeDepth":2,"HasChildren":false,"ParentId":"PTIISTPECO_CH1GEPR","DocOrderId":61,"Children":[],"Data":{"NodeKey":null,"IsUpdated":false,"IsAmended":false,"HasAmendedDescendant":false,"CompareStatus":4,"DocType":1,"DepthOverride":null,"ChunkGroupStartingId":null}},"NextNode":{"Id":"PTIISTPECO_CH1GEPR_S1-3CASEEFHINORE","Heading":"Sec. 1-3. - Catchlines of sections; effect of history notes; references.","NodeDepth":2,"HasChildren":false,"ParentId":"PTIISTPECO_CH1GEPR","DocOrderId":63,"Children":[],"Data":{"NodeKey":null,"IsUpdated":false,"IsAmended":false,"HasAmendedDescendant":false,"CompareStatus":4,"DocType":1,"DepthOverride":null,"ChunkGroupStartingId":null}},"ShowToc":false}